 "_note": [
  "Drives lictor_fuse::fsm::next one row at a time (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md sec 6 table, rows 1-23 plus 17b, plus the",
  "two implicit stay rows and the Idle guard documented in fsm.rs). Config = envelopes/pusht.base.toml compiled",
  "in Enforce mode (k=3 n=5 clear_ticks=5 clamp_streak_to_brake=3 max_clamps=60 stop_confirm=2 brake_timeout=30",
  "rearm=auto rearm_hold=10 max_rearms=2 escalate_after_hold=30 handoff_timeout=200), optionally edited by `cfg`",
  "(clamp_mode, rearm, mode). `rt` overrides counters of a freshly reset FuseRt whose pos is [300, 600]; the hold",
  "latch therefore clamps to [300, 495]. `expect.rt` lists the counters that must hold after the call, `expect.hold`",
  "the latched setpoint, `expect.extra_trips` the bits the FSM raised itself. The test also checks that rt.state",
  "equals `to`, that every row name appears at least once, and that no case is silently unmatched."
 ],
